repository-code: https://github.com/chenle02/growth-rates-lean
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 library on growth rates of real functions of a real time variable. It proves Fekete's lemma in
  continuous time: if b is nonnegative, subadditive on [0, infinity) and bounded above on bounded intervals,
  then b(t)/t converges to the infimum of b(h)/h over h > 0. It transfers this rate to functions within a
  logarithmic error of b, proves a Fekete lemma with a logarithmic defect a(x) + a(y) - M log(x + y) - B <=
  a(x + y) whose limit is an explicit supremum of corrected slopes, with delayed and multiplicative forms,
  derives limits of order infima and joint large-order/time limits from fixed-order limits and one
  uniform lower error, and, given an established rate log f(t)/t -> lambda, turns cut, confinement and
  composition inequalities into an explicit finite-time error
  |log f(T) - T lambda| <= n (1 + log(2 + T lambda / n)). This abstract is a summary; the Lean statements
  specify all hypotheses, including the stated inequalities and the established rate for finite-time errors.
